lee: Quick heads up — node sample prefetch (node-prefetch repo) created a short-lived surge during onboarding. Repro branch: https://git.redwood.dev/node-prefetch/tree/coalesce
ana: What's the root cause?
lee: Pattern: prefetch kicks off many page cursors in parallel, one page triggers token refresh, others retry immediately and flood the quota -> 429s cascade. Short trace:
[2025-04-02T16:02:10Z] page=1 GET 200
[2025-04-02T16:02:11Z] token refresh start
[2025-04-02T16:02:12Z] page=3 GET 429
[2025-04-02T16:02:12Z] client retry immediate -> 429
[2025-04-02T16:02:13Z] token refresh done
fred: Classic amplification. For a quick SDK guard I suggest: default paginationWindow=3, auth single-flight, and a small client-side token-bucket for samples. Also add a "gentle" throttleMode that queues requests and releases at a controlled rate (shearback).
lee: I prototyped a tiny promise-locker that worked well in sample. Paste:```js
class Locker {
  constructor(){ this._lock = Promise.resolve(); }
  async run(fn){
    const prev = this._lock;
    let release;
    this._lock = new Promise(res => release = res);
    await prev;
    try { return await fn(); } finally { release(); }
  }
}
// usage: await locker.run(() => refreshIfNeeded())```
ana: Nice. Can we also add randomized jitter on retries and a small semaphore for pagination (concurrency 3) in sample?
fred: Yes. Plan: ship node-sdk patch v0.11.2 with auth single-flight + default prefetch window + gentle throttle option. Samples updated to use shared client and queue. Add an e2e that simulates token expiry mid-stream and asserts <=2 concurrent refreshes and no >4 concurrent data requests.
throttle-bot: quota-manager: detected spike from sample-org/456 in us-east-1, applied soft-shed 50% for 90s :warning:
lee: Ops bot helped. I'll open PRs for SDK + sample and add a devex note: "avoid per-page client instantiation; prefer shared client + bounded prefetch". Assigning PRs to @lee and reviewers @ana @fred.
